    "The actual per-time pushforward is measurable, normalized, and exactly Gaussian with the internally derived trueMean and trueVariance; this conclusion is reused from the protected genuine finite trajectory law proof.",
    "Generic Gaussian probability measures converge in the official weak topology when real means and true nonnegative variances converge; the proof computes their actual official characteristic functions and applies Mathlib Levy convergence.",
    "The actual recursive marginal laws converge weakly atTop Nat to the genuine invariant stationaryLaw for every real goal/sigma and stable 0<k<2, using the internally derived actual mean and variance limits.",
    "The actual recursively generated states on their varying finite product noise spaces converge in the official TendstoInDistribution sense to the identity random variable under the true stationary Gaussian measure.",
    "Integrals of every bounded continuous real observable under the actual marginal laws converge to its integral under the actual stationary law.",
    "At sigma=0 every actual finite-time state law is Dirac at its derived mean, and these laws converge weakly to Dirac at the goal; zero variance is handled by the same genuine Gaussian characteristic function theorem."
